WEBVTT

1
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.350
"Mi-sung-Li is a rural village
famous for rice and apples."

2
00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.220
"To buy anything,
I have to go into town."

3
00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:07.970
"It takes close to an hour
to go and come back."

4
00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:13.840
KIM TAE-RI

5
00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:19.640
"I came down to my childhood home
from Seoul 3 months ago at winter."

6
00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:28.180
LITTLE FOREST

7
00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:39.970
WINTER

8
00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:45.680
"When it's cold,
I crave dough soup."

9
00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:51.700
"The dough must sit for 2 hours.
Perfect time to clean the snow."

10
00:06:58.990 --> 00:06:59.990
Jae-ha?

11
00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:30.190
"One sip of dough soup
when I'm freezing..."

12
00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:00.010
"There is no more rice
or flour left."

13
00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:05.350
"I have to go into town
or report to my aunt."

14
00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:08.510
Or I could starve.

15
00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.470
"I don't want anyone to know
that I'm here."

16
00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:16.510
Song Hae-won!

17
00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:27.140
"When did you come down?
Why didn't you call!"

18
00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:29.800
"I was going to
after chopping firewood."

19
00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:30.970
Don't lie.

20
00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:32.680
You should've called right away.

21
00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.010
I'll fall!

22
00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:41.510
Welcome home.

23
00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:44.470
I missed you.

24
00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:48.890
"But why'd you come?
Did you pass the exam?"

25
00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:52.970
Why didn't you call me first!

26
00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:55.350
Did your boyfriend pass?

27
00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:56.550
Well, ah...

28
00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:59.220
"Some friends hit you
where it hurts."

29
00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:01.470
Eun-sook is like that.

30
00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:02.550
I get it.

31
00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:05.970
You failed and he passed, huh.

32
00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:10.510
"It hurts your pride
so you came to hide?"

33
00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:13.510
You did that before too!

34
00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:16.140
"- When you did bad on your tests.
- Stop!"

35
00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:18.300
You kept quiet to yourself.

36
00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:21.390
That's why you came, right?

37
00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:25.930
No. I came because I'm hungry.

38
00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:29.010
Not because you're jealous?

39
00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.640
I'm really hungry.

40
00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:37.850
What?

41
00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.930
Should we call Jae-ha over?

42
00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:45.340
Jae-ha?

43
00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:47.850
How long has he been back?

44
00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:53.300
"Jae-ha went to a university nearby
and got a job right away."

45
00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:57.930
"Since I went to school in Seoul,
we naturally lost touch."

46
00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:04.510
"He helped his parents farm
and started a small orchard."

47
00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:06.600
Number 12, please!

48
00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:11.600
"Eun-sook graduated from college
and got a job at the bank in town."

49
00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:18.350
"Since she's never lived away,
she complains how boring it is here."

50
00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:24.850
"Her dream is to escape here
and live in the city."

51
00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:31.590
"I worked and studied for
the teacher certification exam."

52
00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.850
My life in Seoul was stifling too.

53
00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:39.100
Instant food didn't fill me up.

54
00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:45.010
"I meant it when I said
I came back because I'm hungry."

55
00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:46.720
Thanks for the food!

56
00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:03.010
HOON

57
00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:13.300
Hae-won, I passed the exam.

58
00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:17.460
"I don't know how you did,
so I can't really be happy."

59
00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:22.340
Call me. I'll be waiting.

60
00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:47.250
Who is it?

61
00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:15.710
"Wild boars come around
this time of year."

62
00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:22.170
Doesn't the elk cry like humans?

63
00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:27.960
Sounds like a crazy woman crying.

64
00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:36.960
Stop it, Mommy! Please!

65
00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:47.300
AUNT BOK-SOON

66
00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:11.920
What are you doing here?

67
00:13:14.090 --> 00:13:15.300
Aunt Bok-soon?

68
00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:18.960
How'd you know I came?

69
00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:21.500
"There's smoke coming off
your chimney."

70
00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:24.550
I thought your mom was back.

71
00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:27.130
How've you been?

72
00:13:28.630 --> 00:13:30.840
Has Mom been by here?

73
00:13:31.130 --> 00:13:35.960
"I wouldn't know.
I don't come by every day."

74
00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:39.300
"She's not one to come
and say she's back."

75
00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:42.050
Do you keep in touch?

76
00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:45.500
Oh dear.

77
00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:48.210
You're just like her.

78
00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:49.000
What?

79
00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:54.090
"I thought your mom was odd.
You're unique too."

80
00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:57.340
You're so much like her.

81
00:13:57.380 --> 00:13:59.670
Of course, she's dad's sister.

82
00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:04.630
"Come have breakfast
and take some food."

83
00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:07.620
It's okay. I'm not staying long.

84
00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.330
When are you leaving?

85
00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.250
In 3 or 4 days.

86
00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:18.700
"If Mom ever comes back,
don't tell her I was here."

87
00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:22.450
"- Please?
- Okay..."

88
00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:26.950
Come on. Let's go.

89
00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:39.790
Eat slowly. You'll choke.

90
00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:46.200
Why do you look so haggard?

91
00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.330
Eat slowly!

92
00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.040
"- But it's good!
- Why you..."

93
00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:55.370
Try the pickle too.

94
00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:13.330
"-Long time no see.
-Long time..."

95
00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:19.580
What's the dog for?

96
00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:24.160
Here.

97
00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.450
Sleeping alone can be scary.

98
00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:35.500
"How's this going to console me?
I'll go back soon anyway."

99
00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.750
"Warm, living things
are comforting."

100
00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:42.790
"If you're leaving soon,
why bring all that food?"

101
00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:45.580
See ya.

102
00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:51.450
"His name's Fivo!
He was the fifth one born."

103
00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:58.750
Wait! Take him back!

104
00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:30.120
"Sorry, Hoon.
I'll be in touch soon..."

105
00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:47.950
Hey!

106
00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:11.080
"A few days after
my college entrance exams..."

107
00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:13.250
Mom! I'm hungry!

108
00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:18.700
Mom?

109
00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:25.790
Mom!

110
00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:29.910
Mom?

111
00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:35.290
Mom?

112
00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.120
"- Hi, Aunt Bok-soon.
- Hi."

113
00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:56.390
"Where'd your mom go?
Didn't she say anything?"

114
00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:03.050
"She came by earlier
and asked me to watch you."

115
00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:08.470
"She didn't say why.
She just left after saying that."

116
00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:13.260
Did you eat?

117
00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:17.890
I'm not hungry.

118
00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:23.930
"You didn't even graduate yet.
She's crazy!"

119
00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:31.350
"Don't worry.
She'll be back soon."

120
00:18:33.930 --> 00:18:35.180
I doubt it.

121
00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:41.260
Oh dear.

122
00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:16.680
"In her hidden letter,
she wrote about why she left."

123
00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:21.260
"But I couldn't understand
any of it."

124
00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:27.010
"I just knew that
she wouldn't be back soon."

125
00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:32.470
"We moved to Dad's hometown
when I was 4 years old."

126
00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:40.760
"It was because Dad was sick,
but we stayed even after he died."

127
00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:49.760
"I was angry and curious
about Mom leaving so suddenly."

128
00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:54.720
"I wanted to live well
and prove I didn't need her."

129
00:19:56.930 --> 00:19:58.760
Here, Hae-won!

130
00:19:58.970 --> 00:20:00.720
Looks like good news.

131
00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:08.930
ACCEPTANCE LETTER

132
00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:25.720
"Only I came back
without finding answers."

133
00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:29.730
I wonder if Mom found hers.

134
00:21:07.210 --> 00:21:10.750
Come here, Fivo.

135
00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:33.000
Hey, where are you going?

136
00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:36.750
Can you mash the red beans?

137
00:21:36.840 --> 00:21:39.670
Hey, I'm a guest here.

138
00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:42.750
Bang! Bang!

139
00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:47.130
How can you put a guest to work?

140
00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:50.800
What's this?

141
00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:52.880
Am I doing this right?

142
00:21:55.130 --> 00:21:56.210
Yup.

143
00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:57.710
You're doing good!

144
00:21:58.340 --> 00:21:59.460
Yes, ma'am.

145
00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:08.000
It's all mashed up!

146
00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:11.590
Now, what do I do?

147
00:22:27.840 --> 00:22:28.840
So colorful!

148
00:22:52.190 --> 00:22:53.730
Fivo! Fivo!

149
00:22:54.190 --> 00:22:55.940
Sit Fivo!

150
00:22:56.230 --> 00:22:57.100
Fivo sit!

151
00:22:57.100 --> 00:22:58.730
Give me your paw!

152
00:22:58.730 --> 00:22:59.730
Good dog.

153
00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:07.230
Is it done?

154
00:23:07.230 --> 00:23:08.770
Almost.

155
00:23:10.980 --> 00:23:12.770
"- Not bad, huh?
- What?"

156
00:23:13.310 --> 00:23:15.310
"Jae-ha.
What do you think?"

157
00:23:21.350 --> 00:23:22.940
You mean as a man?

158
00:23:25.600 --> 00:23:27.850
Didn't we call him 'Snotty'?

159
00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:30.650
You see him as a man now?

160
00:23:31.560 --> 00:23:33.560
You gave him the nickname!

161
00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:38.650
"Well, there's no other guy
in this village."

162
00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:41.350
He's cute.

163
00:23:43.440 --> 00:23:44.690
I'm not interested.

164
00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:48.520
"Damn dating...
It's the same in the city and here."

165
00:23:49.270 --> 00:23:53.520
"Then, keep your eyes off him.
He's mine."

166
00:23:53.940 --> 00:23:55.150
Got that?

167
00:24:08.900 --> 00:24:10.900
"- Hey!
- What?"

168
00:24:11.190 --> 00:24:12.400
Don't!

169
00:24:13.730 --> 00:24:14.900
There.

170
00:24:19.690 --> 00:24:21.350
Tada!

171
00:24:21.440 --> 00:24:23.150
How can you make rice cake?

172
00:24:30.480 --> 00:24:33.440
"It tastes just like
your mom's rice cake."

173
00:24:34.520 --> 00:24:36.350
I think mine tastes better.

174
00:24:37.440 --> 00:24:39.850
But it's slightly different.

175
00:24:40.520 --> 00:24:41.520
How?

176
00:24:41.770 --> 00:24:46.690
Your mom's tasted a bit sweeter.

177
00:24:47.520 --> 00:24:50.690
Yours tastes slightly saltier.

178
00:24:52.850 --> 00:24:56.150
"How do you remember that?
I think it tastes good."

179
00:24:56.730 --> 00:24:58.310
How did he know?

180
00:24:58.850 --> 00:25:03.440
"Mom used pumpkin instead of
gardenia, so it'll be sweeter."

181
00:25:04.190 --> 00:25:11.060
"And I put a little more salt
in boiling the red beans."

182
00:25:13.620 --> 00:25:16.290
It's cold! Watch the furnace.

183
00:25:21.290 --> 00:25:23.540
"- You said you'd sleep over.
- When?"

184
00:25:27.120 --> 00:25:28.580
Will you drive me home?

185
00:25:29.790 --> 00:25:31.200
You live down the street.

186
00:25:31.450 --> 00:25:35.660
"There's no streetlamp!
I can't see in the dark."

187
00:25:36.790 --> 00:25:38.700
"Let Fivo sleep outside
when it warms up."

188
00:25:39.080 --> 00:25:41.080
I said I'm going back soon.

189
00:25:41.250 --> 00:25:43.250
What's to do in Seoul?

190
00:25:43.790 --> 00:25:47.870
"You failed your test, quit your job,
and don't talk to your boyfriend."

191
00:25:49.450 --> 00:25:50.620
Don't go anywhere!

192
00:25:52.790 --> 00:25:53.790
Let's go!

193
00:25:55.790 --> 00:25:57.200
I'll come tomorrow.

194
00:25:57.370 --> 00:25:59.290
Reserve a seat for me at 7.

195
00:25:59.660 --> 00:26:02.120
"- It's cold. Let's go.
- Hey!"

196
00:26:02.200 --> 00:26:04.160
"- Why you!
- Hey!"

197
00:26:05.080 --> 00:26:06.080
Silly.

198
00:26:16.290 --> 00:26:17.700
That's weird.

199
00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:19.580
"- What?
- I don't get it."

200
00:26:20.580 --> 00:26:21.750
Hae-won.

201
00:26:22.790 --> 00:26:27.160
"She doesn't look for her mom.
They were really close."

202
00:26:28.790 --> 00:26:29.910
It's her pride.

203
00:26:31.250 --> 00:26:34.120
"She must be curious
and angry at her."

204
00:26:35.080 --> 00:26:39.540
"But if she expresses that,
she thinks she'd be losing."

205
00:26:40.750 --> 00:26:44.750
"She planned to move out
right after high school graduation."

206
00:26:45.620 --> 00:26:47.370
But her mom beat her to it!

207
00:26:48.000 --> 00:26:50.000
It hurt her pride.

208
00:26:51.250 --> 00:26:53.000
Moms and daughters are like that?

209
00:26:53.330 --> 00:26:55.500
"It's because
they're mother and daughter."

210
00:26:56.040 --> 00:26:58.080
Hae-won is a proud girl.

211
00:27:00.200 --> 00:27:03.120
"She probably fought
with her boyfriend because of that."

212
00:27:03.410 --> 00:27:05.750
She broke up with her boyfriend?

213
00:27:09.280 --> 00:27:10.950
I don't know.

214
00:27:16.650 --> 00:27:19.070
I'll be back soon. Don't worry.

215
00:27:19.490 --> 00:27:20.700
When?

216
00:27:22.200 --> 00:27:23.900
Maybe a week or so.

217
00:27:26.950 --> 00:27:28.820
I'll call when I get there.

218
00:27:29.240 --> 00:27:30.530
Why are you there?

219
00:27:30.530 --> 00:27:33.070
Hello? I can't hear you!

220
00:27:33.070 --> 00:27:33.740
Hello?

221
00:27:33.740 --> 00:27:36.240
"The signal's weak here
in the country!"

222
00:27:36.240 --> 00:27:39.450
"- Hello?
- I'll call you back later!"

223
00:27:45.780 --> 00:27:46.990
Song Hae-won.

224
00:27:48.490 --> 00:27:51.360
Why's your life so hard?

225
00:27:58.650 --> 00:28:03.360
Your life is hard too, huh?

226
00:28:51.990 --> 00:28:52.990
Thief!

227
00:28:54.110 --> 00:28:55.610
It's a burglar!

228
00:28:55.990 --> 00:28:57.780
Thief! Thief!

229
00:29:00.240 --> 00:29:01.610
You scared me.

230
00:29:02.030 --> 00:29:03.860
Why'd you sneak into my field?

231
00:29:06.450 --> 00:29:07.740
Good tomatoes, huh?

232
00:29:09.820 --> 00:29:12.860
"So sweet.
The ones in Seoul tasted flat."

233
00:29:12.990 --> 00:29:15.150
"Freshly picked ones
are different."

234
00:29:18.400 --> 00:29:20.530
Look at you!

235
00:29:21.740 --> 00:29:22.740
What?

236
00:29:22.860 --> 00:29:26.320
"I'm proud of you.
Where'd you learn to farm?"

237
00:29:28.450 --> 00:29:31.070
My dad, the other farmers,

238
00:29:32.150 --> 00:29:33.150
and Internet.

239
00:29:36.240 --> 00:29:40.360
"Little girl, watch what you say
to an adult, huh?"

240
00:29:41.650 --> 00:29:45.700
"My birthday is way earlier
than yours!"

241
00:29:46.700 --> 00:29:48.200
Hey, your scar is gone.

242
00:29:48.740 --> 00:29:49.740
What?

243
00:29:50.110 --> 00:29:53.280
"Remember when you tried to catch
tomatoes with your mouth?"

244
00:29:54.200 --> 00:29:57.990
"You fell over there, cut your head,
and bled so much."

245
00:29:58.650 --> 00:30:00.900
"We got so shocked
and cried with you!"

246
00:30:00.900 --> 00:30:02.900
Right! Where was it?

247
00:30:02.950 --> 00:30:04.950
I was so scared then.

248
00:30:05.900 --> 00:30:07.990
How about it for old time's sake?

249
00:30:08.030 --> 00:30:09.030
Catch!

250
00:30:12.700 --> 00:30:14.070
Can't you catch it?

251
00:30:14.070 --> 00:30:15.200
Come here you!

252
00:30:15.240 --> 00:30:16.320
Lost your touch?

253
00:30:16.980 --> 00:30:18.560
Okay! I'm ready!

254
00:30:18.650 --> 00:30:19.730
"- Catch!
- Okay."

255
00:30:23.560 --> 00:30:27.060
"- Try it again! Ready?
- No way!"

256
00:30:27.190 --> 00:30:28.230
Catch!

257
00:30:30.100 --> 00:30:31.350
I'll get you!

258
00:30:36.520 --> 00:30:38.520
One, two!

259
00:30:40.270 --> 00:30:41.270
Timber!

260
00:30:58.980 --> 00:31:01.560
"After a good sweat,
you need alcohol."

261
00:31:18.520 --> 00:31:22.770
"On long winter nights,
Mom sometimes made Makgeolli."

262
00:31:24.100 --> 00:31:27.190
"Sikhye for Hae-won.
Makgeolli for me."

263
00:31:27.730 --> 00:31:28.730
Cheers!

264
00:31:29.190 --> 00:31:30.190
Cheers!

265
00:31:36.230 --> 00:31:37.480
Is it good?

266
00:31:38.400 --> 00:31:39.600
Wanna try it?

267
00:31:39.690 --> 00:31:40.690
Yes!

268
00:31:43.480 --> 00:31:46.060
"It tasted sour, acidic,
and adult-like."

269
00:31:46.520 --> 00:31:48.520
It's gross!

270
00:32:32.480 --> 00:32:37.440
"Malt makes it into sweet rice punch,
but yeast turns it into wine."

271
00:33:13.900 --> 00:33:15.060
It's perfect!

272
00:33:15.980 --> 00:33:19.850
"It's best to drink it with
some company in the cold."

273
00:33:26.190 --> 00:33:27.690
It's really good!

274
00:33:30.510 --> 00:33:32.510
"- It's cold! Close the door!
- No!"

275
00:33:32.720 --> 00:33:34.930
"You have to drink Makgeolli
with the cold wind!"

276
00:33:35.180 --> 00:33:38.470
"Cut the nonsense
and close the door!"

277
00:33:39.510 --> 00:33:40.510
No way!

278
00:33:50.350 --> 00:33:52.010
"- What was that?
- No idea."

279
00:33:52.010 --> 00:33:53.600
"- What did I trip on?
- Don't know."

280
00:33:53.640 --> 00:33:55.090
Fess up now!

281
00:33:55.100 --> 00:33:58.050
"- Why you!
- You wanna die!"

282
00:34:00.180 --> 00:34:01.180
Stop!

283
00:34:02.350 --> 00:34:04.510
Stop it!

284
00:34:08.430 --> 00:34:10.260
What are you doing?

285
00:34:11.470 --> 00:34:12.470
Hi!

286
00:34:12.640 --> 00:34:13.680
What are you doing?

287
00:34:13.680 --> 00:34:17.140
"Can't you see
I'm parking my bike?"

288
00:34:19.550 --> 00:34:22.220
"Is Jae-ha here?
You called him too?"

289
00:34:22.600 --> 00:34:24.600
Thought I only called you over?

290
00:34:27.180 --> 00:34:29.510
It's not that.

291
00:34:30.180 --> 00:34:31.180
Hey.

292
00:34:31.390 --> 00:34:32.390
Hi.

293
00:34:33.550 --> 00:34:35.550
She pushed me so hard!

294
00:34:36.010 --> 00:34:37.010
Move!

295
00:34:37.760 --> 00:34:39.010
It hurts!

296
00:34:39.390 --> 00:34:40.640
It's freezing.

297
00:34:41.100 --> 00:34:42.760
"- Move!
- Hey!"

298
00:34:43.350 --> 00:34:44.800
Cheers!

299
00:34:53.300 --> 00:34:54.300
It's so good!

300
00:34:56.180 --> 00:34:57.550
You drank it one shot?

301
00:34:59.800 --> 00:35:01.970
"Because you came,
the three of us can drink."

302
00:35:02.800 --> 00:35:04.930
"Is it our first time
drinking together?"

303
00:35:05.640 --> 00:35:07.390
"- I guess.
- Right."

304
00:35:09.390 --> 00:35:14.640
"But why come down
when I said I want to go up?"

305
00:35:15.970 --> 00:35:19.800
"I was sick of working at a store.
It pays peanuts."

306
00:35:20.800 --> 00:35:22.930
I love drip coffee,

307
00:35:22.930 --> 00:35:25.100
"but I can't even afford
to buy it."

308
00:35:25.260 --> 00:35:27.760
"Right.
The coffee there is different."

309
00:35:28.720 --> 00:35:30.930
"- It's expensive.
- Right."

310
00:35:32.680 --> 00:35:34.430
"Do you know
what drip coffee is?"

311
00:35:36.760 --> 00:35:37.760
Of course.

312
00:35:38.640 --> 00:35:42.140
She doesn't. I can tell.

313
00:35:42.220 --> 00:35:43.300
Just one more glass please.

314
00:35:43.300 --> 00:35:45.970
"- Stop drinking!
- I'm not drunk!"

315
00:35:46.470 --> 00:35:47.890
That's enough.

316
00:35:48.050 --> 00:35:49.050
Hey! Hey!

317
00:35:50.640 --> 00:35:52.640
Are you sleeping?

318
00:35:55.390 --> 00:35:59.050
"I'm cold.
Aren't you cold?"

319
00:36:09.300 --> 00:36:12.390
"Living in the city,
I could see..."

320
00:36:13.350 --> 00:36:16.010
how great a job farming is.

321
00:36:18.480 --> 00:36:23.810
The sprouts in the spring...

322
00:36:33.100 --> 00:36:44.150
"they look up at the holy sky
like small earthly spirits..."

323
00:36:45.190 --> 00:36:48.350
I can't really describe it...

324
00:36:53.980 --> 00:36:58.770
"But I think I chose
an incredibly cool job."

325
00:37:00.480 --> 00:37:03.150
"Jae-ha is cool
when he's drunk."

326
00:37:05.060 --> 00:37:07.350
He came back here with an answer.

327
00:37:08.230 --> 00:37:09.230
But.

328
00:37:09.520 --> 00:37:13.350
"I couldn't bear it anymore
and ran away here."

329
00:37:15.690 --> 00:37:16.690
Hello.

330
00:37:16.770 --> 00:37:18.400
"1 pork and
1 ham and cheese, please."

331
00:37:18.440 --> 00:37:19.940
One moment, please.

332
00:37:25.020 --> 00:37:26.690
Hey! Stop!

333
00:37:34.770 --> 00:37:38.310
"It's not fair to go back
after just winter here, right?"

334
00:37:40.650 --> 00:37:41.730
Am I right or not?

335
00:37:42.480 --> 00:37:43.480
Huh?

336
00:37:43.730 --> 00:37:44.770
Tell me.

337
00:37:45.650 --> 00:37:46.650
Huh?

338
00:37:54.770 --> 00:37:59.190
"If I stay till the spring's spirits
break through the winter,"

339
00:37:59.850 --> 00:38:01.770
will I find my answers?

340
00:38:09.980 --> 00:38:17.900
SPRING

341
00:38:35.100 --> 00:38:36.600
Thanks for the food!

342
00:38:38.440 --> 00:38:41.230
"Potatoes are planted first
in spring."

343
00:38:42.520 --> 00:38:46.810
"Though it's cold, the ground's warmth
pushes the potato sprouts out."

344
00:38:47.150 --> 00:38:50.650
"The sprouts, the flowers,
and bearing crop..."

345
00:38:51.350 --> 00:38:53.190
It all takes time.

346
00:38:54.810 --> 00:38:55.810
You have to wait.

347
00:38:56.730 --> 00:38:57.940
You must wait.

348
00:38:58.690 --> 00:38:59.690
Wait.

349
00:39:00.440 --> 00:39:04.150
"You have to wait to taste
the best food."

350
00:39:05.440 --> 00:39:11.400
"You can get spring greens for free,
but potatoes take hard work."

351
00:39:58.440 --> 00:40:02.440
"Spring bracken must be carefully
dried and stored to eat in the fall."

352
00:40:06.560 --> 00:40:08.690
I talk as if I'll stay till fall.

353
00:40:36.400 --> 00:40:40.560
"When potato sprouts come up,
it's time to plant other crops."

354
00:40:43.900 --> 00:40:47.310
"From then on,
there's no time to waste on the farm."

355
00:40:54.940 --> 00:40:57.350
"- Are these peppers?
- Hot peppers."

356
00:40:57.400 --> 00:40:59.940
"- I'll take $3 worth, please.
- Sure."

357
00:41:04.520 --> 00:41:06.600
"Eun-sook!
You're planting it wrong."

358
00:41:07.100 --> 00:41:08.310
It's right!

359
00:41:09.810 --> 00:41:11.650
They're too close together!

360
00:41:15.940 --> 00:41:19.230
"- Plant 'em again.
- No! Go away!"

361
00:41:20.230 --> 00:41:23.600
"If you plant 'em like this,
they'll get tangled up!"

362
00:41:23.650 --> 00:41:24.690
"- Move!
- No!"

363
00:41:24.690 --> 00:41:27.310
Shut up and just go home.

364
00:41:28.980 --> 00:41:31.230
"- It's your fault.
- You go home."

365
00:41:31.310 --> 00:41:34.520
"- No! You go home!
- Shut up. Be quiet!"

366
00:41:34.690 --> 00:41:37.650
"- What?
- Watch. Try it again."

367
00:41:57.900 --> 00:41:59.440
Thanks for the food!

368
00:42:31.520 --> 00:42:35.350
"Aren't you scared to live there
with no cameras or door locks?"

369
00:42:36.730 --> 00:42:39.230
What will you do all day?

370
00:42:41.110 --> 00:42:43.070
"I hate the country
because of bugs!"

371
00:42:43.110 --> 00:42:45.950
"Flies, worms, and bees!
Gross!"

372
00:42:46.610 --> 00:42:47.690
What? Why?

373
00:42:47.700 --> 00:42:48.490
It's a bug!

374
00:42:48.490 --> 00:42:50.530
No!

375
00:42:53.150 --> 00:42:55.200
Why hello, caterpillar!

376
00:42:56.280 --> 00:42:57.900
Did it fall from the tree?

377
00:42:58.030 --> 00:42:59.700
"- You touched it?
- Amazing!"

378
00:43:00.490 --> 00:43:05.450
"They don't know that I'm a product
of the land and air here."

379
00:43:10.030 --> 00:43:12.360
"Of course,
some things are annoying."

380
00:43:12.360 --> 00:43:13.610
"Fivo, Fivo!
What's this? Look!"

381
00:43:13.610 --> 00:43:14.700
Hae-won!

382
00:43:15.110 --> 00:43:16.320
Eat it!

383
00:43:18.110 --> 00:43:19.150
Mr. Kim!

384
00:43:20.320 --> 00:43:23.070
"Hae-won?
Come have a seat here."

385
00:43:24.280 --> 00:43:25.150
Come here.

386
00:43:25.150 --> 00:43:28.450
"You want to be a teacher?
Did you pass the exam?"

387
00:43:28.900 --> 00:43:30.320
Got a boyfriend?

388
00:43:31.820 --> 00:43:36.400
"What happened to your mom?
Did she get remarried?"

389
00:43:36.650 --> 00:43:39.780
"So what if she did!
I'd get remarried too!"

390
00:43:54.610 --> 00:43:56.610
"CLOSED TO HELP OUT
IN FARMING SEASON"

391
00:43:57.360 --> 00:43:59.400
The most annoying thing is.

392
00:44:01.490 --> 00:44:03.820
"Mom coming to mind
whenever I cook."

393
00:44:05.150 --> 00:44:08.070
"It's like I'm always
competing with her."

394
00:44:08.650 --> 00:44:09.860
Focus.

395
00:44:11.030 --> 00:44:13.610
Cooking reflects your heart.

396
00:44:15.820 --> 00:44:18.450
Please get out of my head, Mom.

397
00:44:41.820 --> 00:44:43.650
It's best to eat it raw,

398
00:44:44.360 --> 00:44:47.450
"but I want to make
something unique."

399
00:44:47.650 --> 00:44:49.530
Not again!

400
00:44:50.400 --> 00:44:51.780
How about pancake?

401
00:44:52.400 --> 00:44:54.360
Cabbage pancake?

402
00:45:18.110 --> 00:45:19.200
Lots!

403
00:45:19.740 --> 00:45:21.820
Swirl it on.

404
00:45:22.900 --> 00:45:24.070
Like this.

405
00:45:26.320 --> 00:45:27.320
Wanna try?

406
00:45:40.400 --> 00:45:41.490
What's that?

407
00:45:43.530 --> 00:45:44.530
Tree.

408
00:45:45.030 --> 00:45:46.110
Tree branch.

409
00:45:46.280 --> 00:45:48.610
I'll shred this on top.

410
00:45:49.070 --> 00:45:50.070
What?

411
00:45:50.820 --> 00:45:52.030
That's weird!

412
00:45:52.820 --> 00:45:55.700
Don't do it Mommy!

413
00:45:56.030 --> 00:45:58.030
No tree branch!

414
00:46:03.530 --> 00:46:04.700
All done!

415
00:46:05.110 --> 00:46:06.490
It's weird!

416
00:46:06.490 --> 00:46:09.030
Look! The tree bits are moving!

417
00:46:12.950 --> 00:46:14.360
Wanna smell it?

418
00:46:16.360 --> 00:46:20.030
"It smelled really unique
and original."

419
00:46:20.200 --> 00:46:22.650
"- Looks good, huh?
- I thought she was a genius."

420
00:46:27.570 --> 00:46:29.570
This looks so good!

421
00:46:30.490 --> 00:46:32.200
Mom didn't create that?

422
00:46:32.860 --> 00:46:34.360
It's delicious!

423
00:46:34.770 --> 00:46:36.060
Excuse me?

424
00:46:37.310 --> 00:46:43.150
"Sometimes I knew she lied,
but Mom's cooking was never boring."

425
00:46:45.690 --> 00:46:47.690
Unique dishes are good,

426
00:46:47.940 --> 00:46:50.190
"but spring cabbage
tastes best raw."

427
00:46:50.850 --> 00:46:53.400
"The more you chew,
the sweeter it gets."

428
00:47:43.270 --> 00:47:46.480
"I haven't delivered to this place
in a while."

429
00:47:46.940 --> 00:47:48.270
Hae-won, right?

430
00:47:48.270 --> 00:47:49.850
Yes. Hello, sir.

431
00:47:50.480 --> 00:47:53.940
Wait! Could you send this back?

432
00:47:54.650 --> 00:47:55.650
Why?

433
00:47:55.940 --> 00:47:56.940
Because...

434
00:47:58.150 --> 00:48:02.100
"I'm going back soon.
I don't want mail coming here."

435
00:48:02.900 --> 00:48:03.940
I can't do that.

436
00:48:04.310 --> 00:48:07.020
"There's no address.
It can't be returned."

437
00:48:07.480 --> 00:48:08.560
And Hae-won,

438
00:48:09.150 --> 00:48:14.690
"it's your freedom to read it or not,
but I must deliver it."

439
00:48:16.020 --> 00:48:20.190
That's a mail carrier's fate.

440
00:49:22.900 --> 00:49:25.350
So? What did it say?

441
00:49:29.980 --> 00:49:31.560
What did your mom write?

442
00:49:33.310 --> 00:49:34.730
Her potato bread recipe.

443
00:49:37.150 --> 00:49:41.100
"I was dying to know.
You tried Mom's potato bread, right?"

444
00:49:41.940 --> 00:49:43.480
It was the best!

445
00:49:48.060 --> 00:49:51.100
"I begged her to tell me,
but she said she'd teach me later."

446
00:49:56.100 --> 00:50:00.350
"She leaves home and sends me
her potato bread recipe?"

447
00:50:00.980 --> 00:50:02.020
How could she?

448
00:50:02.550 --> 00:50:04.100
It's nice and useful.

449
00:50:10.300 --> 00:50:13.010
"Then write her back
with a unique recipe of your own."

450
00:50:17.640 --> 00:50:19.300
I don't know where she is.

451
00:50:23.600 --> 00:50:25.600
I think she's living fine.

452
00:50:30.640 --> 00:50:35.720
"That's weird.
How did she know I was here?"

453
00:51:45.890 --> 00:51:53.800
SUMMER

454
00:52:25.390 --> 00:52:28.100
"No matter how much
I pluck the weed out,"

455
00:52:28.510 --> 00:52:30.720
it grows like my worries.

456
00:52:33.930 --> 00:52:35.850
It's way too hot.

457
00:52:43.640 --> 00:52:44.680
Thanks.

458
00:52:45.970 --> 00:52:46.970
No thanks.

459
00:52:47.220 --> 00:52:48.760
"-It's nice and cold.
-I'm good."

460
00:52:49.510 --> 00:52:51.220
"-It's hot, isn't it?
-Thank you."

461
00:52:51.470 --> 00:52:53.350
"-Iced coffee?
-Thank you."

462
00:53:05.760 --> 00:53:07.600
We fought over nothing.

463
00:53:08.100 --> 00:53:11.390
"Eun-sook complained non-stop
about her bank manager."

464
00:53:11.470 --> 00:53:13.930
"He always wanders around
outside."

465
00:53:14.600 --> 00:53:17.470
"Then he shows up late
when we're about to close"

466
00:53:18.180 --> 00:53:20.640
"and tells us
to do the work over again!"

467
00:53:21.100 --> 00:53:23.100
"Why doesn't he tell us
in the first place?"

468
00:53:24.970 --> 00:53:27.890
"If I keep working here,
I'll get cancer and die!"

469
00:53:29.020 --> 00:53:30.520
Then just quit.

470
00:53:33.900 --> 00:53:37.520
"If it stresses you out that much,
it's better for you to quit."

471
00:53:39.940 --> 00:53:41.230
How could you?

472
00:53:42.770 --> 00:53:43.770
What?

473
00:53:44.230 --> 00:53:46.270
How can you tell me to quit?

474
00:53:46.770 --> 00:53:48.770
You don't care at all, do you?

475
00:53:52.600 --> 00:53:54.600
What did I say?

476
00:53:55.770 --> 00:53:59.440
"Why would I stress out about it
if I'm just going to quit?"

477
00:54:00.230 --> 00:54:02.810
Is quitting that easy to you?

478
00:54:03.980 --> 00:54:08.690
"A friend should take my side
and pat my back."

479
00:54:10.270 --> 00:54:14.230
But you act all high and mighty?

480
00:54:15.900 --> 00:54:18.940
"I can never talk to you!
You don't listen!"

481
00:54:19.560 --> 00:54:20.900
You're frustrating!

482
00:54:22.400 --> 00:54:23.980
So suffocating!

483
00:54:30.810 --> 00:54:31.940
What's with her?

484
00:54:35.190 --> 00:54:36.810
She'll come around.

485
00:54:38.350 --> 00:54:39.980
But it bothers me.

486
00:54:40.810 --> 00:54:42.310
This isn't like you.

487
00:54:43.190 --> 00:54:45.900
"Remember when you were
bullied in grade 4?"

488
00:54:47.600 --> 00:54:48.600
Me?

489
00:54:49.520 --> 00:54:50.810
You don't remember?

490
00:54:51.310 --> 00:54:52.810
I was really surprised by you.

491
00:54:54.350 --> 00:54:56.770
"Other kids would've cried
and had a hard time."

492
00:54:57.650 --> 00:55:00.730
"But you didn't care
and just let them be."

493
00:55:02.270 --> 00:55:05.440
"It's like you ignored them
instead of them leaving you out."

494
00:55:06.810 --> 00:55:08.810
Soon, they stopped bullying you.

495
00:55:10.480 --> 00:55:11.480
Really?

496
00:55:13.900 --> 00:55:16.560
"I thought you were cool.
Don't remember?"

497
00:55:18.190 --> 00:55:19.400
Not really.

498
00:55:21.100 --> 00:55:24.520
"It was Yong-hyun, Min-seok,
and Soon-chun."

499
00:55:25.310 --> 00:55:27.310
Yong-hyun is a farmer here.

500
00:55:27.350 --> 00:55:30.520
"Soon-chun runs a pizza shop
in Seoul."

501
00:55:31.600 --> 00:55:33.230
I wonder what Min-seok is up to.

502
00:55:34.900 --> 00:55:36.230
I remembered.

503
00:55:37.020 --> 00:55:39.310
Mom? Kids are bullying me.

504
00:55:41.060 --> 00:55:42.060
What?

505
00:55:42.440 --> 00:55:43.480
Why?

506
00:55:43.650 --> 00:55:44.810
I don't know.

507
00:55:45.400 --> 00:55:51.770
"They don't answer me
or let me play with them."

508
00:55:54.440 --> 00:55:55.770
Just leave them.

509
00:55:55.770 --> 00:55:56.770
What?

510
00:55:57.060 --> 00:55:58.400
If you respond to that,

511
00:55:58.980 --> 00:56:01.810
"they'll get excited
and do it more."

512
00:56:07.900 --> 00:56:08.900
What?

513
00:56:09.520 --> 00:56:14.310
"I'm upset, but you talk
as if it is nothing!"

514
00:56:15.650 --> 00:56:17.810
You should console me!

515
00:56:19.270 --> 00:56:22.190
"Know what those bullies
want the most?"

516
00:56:24.650 --> 00:56:26.150
To see you sad.

517
00:56:26.900 --> 00:56:30.150
So, if you don't get sad,

518
00:56:32.150 --> 00:56:33.940
you win!

519
00:56:36.520 --> 00:56:37.690
Turn around.

520
00:56:40.850 --> 00:56:42.480
Number 21, please.

521
00:56:52.230 --> 00:56:53.230
Hey!

522
00:56:54.560 --> 00:56:55.650
What's this?

523
00:57:01.190 --> 00:57:04.310
La joie de vivre crème brulee.

524
00:57:05.190 --> 00:57:06.690
Crème brulee for short.

525
00:58:01.850 --> 00:58:02.850
Here.

526
00:58:05.270 --> 00:58:06.270
Hit it!

527
00:58:08.730 --> 00:58:10.770
Mom was like a magician.

528
00:58:11.650 --> 00:58:14.770
"A magician who can change
my mood instantly."

529
00:58:14.850 --> 00:58:17.650
This is called crème brulee.

530
00:58:18.430 --> 00:58:20.100
Crème brulee.

531
00:58:20.720 --> 00:58:23.760
"I created it.
It's actually called,."

532
00:58:24.470 --> 00:58:27.510
La joie de vivre crème brulee.

533
00:58:28.550 --> 00:58:32.140
"But I shortened it to crème brulee
just for you."

534
00:58:32.430 --> 00:58:34.390
Crème brulee-lee-lee-lee.

535
00:58:34.390 --> 00:58:35.930
Brulee-lee-lee?

536
00:58:40.180 --> 00:58:42.970
Village chief here.

537
00:58:43.800 --> 00:58:46.550
There's a heat wave warning again.

538
00:58:47.390 --> 00:58:52.680
"While Granny Kim Yong-lae
picked peppers yesterday afternoon,"

539
00:58:52.800 --> 00:58:57.010
"she fell from heatstroke
and almost died."

540
00:58:57.890 --> 00:59:04.800
"Please refrain from farming
in daytime and drink lots of water."

541
00:59:05.390 --> 00:59:06.470
Thank you.

542
00:59:12.050 --> 00:59:13.590
Stop!

543
00:59:13.600 --> 00:59:15.510
"I'm watering the jujube tree.
Look!"

544
01:00:33.510 --> 01:00:34.510
I'm hot.

545
01:00:36.850 --> 01:00:41.390
"I'm fine sitting still like this.
There's a nice breeze."

546
01:00:45.720 --> 01:00:47.850
"- What breeze?
- Oh my!"

547
01:00:47.890 --> 01:00:49.890
What's with all the weed?

548
01:00:52.640 --> 01:00:55.930
"You can't tell
if it's a melon field or not."

549
01:00:56.430 --> 01:00:58.430
I'll pluck the weed later.

550
01:00:58.850 --> 01:01:02.470
"Why do it later?
It's best to do it now."

551
01:01:03.350 --> 01:01:07.010
"- Don't muck around and work!
- Yes, ma'am."

552
01:01:10.720 --> 01:01:14.970
Granny didn't pass away, did she?

553
01:01:17.720 --> 01:01:19.600
Why would my mom die so soon?

554
01:01:24.300 --> 01:01:28.220
"Why don't you call her?
Stop being so stubborn."

555
01:01:33.180 --> 01:01:38.640
"She was against me marrying your dad,
so I stormed out"

556
01:01:39.550 --> 01:01:41.680
saying I'll prove her wrong.

557
01:01:42.720 --> 01:01:44.430
I can totally picture it.

558
01:01:47.140 --> 01:01:50.640
Don't you want to date again?

559
01:01:55.010 --> 01:01:56.430
Just wondering.

560
01:01:57.050 --> 01:02:01.390
I hope it's not because of me...

561
01:02:03.760 --> 01:02:05.180
You've matured.

562
01:02:08.180 --> 01:02:09.180
It is because of me?

563
01:02:15.420 --> 01:02:20.210
"If I wanted to date,
I would have."

564
01:02:22.670 --> 01:02:28.920
"I dated long enough with your dad,
I don't miss it at all."

565
01:02:33.710 --> 01:02:35.170
Do you miss dad?

566
01:02:49.590 --> 01:02:53.090
"Even if it's thrown like that,
tomatoes will grow next year."

567
01:02:56.250 --> 01:02:57.340
It's amazing.

568
01:03:23.090 --> 01:03:26.840
"In order for it to grow
just by throwing it like that,"

569
01:03:27.090 --> 01:03:32.300
"it must be a ripe tomato
grown outdoors with plenty of sun."

570
01:03:43.460 --> 01:03:45.460
She meant she missed him.

571
01:03:48.960 --> 01:03:50.960
Tomatoes are weak to rain.

572
01:03:51.590 --> 01:03:57.500
"If it rains too much, the stem
turns brown and withers."

573
01:03:58.960 --> 01:04:02.050
"It's a hit or miss
to grow tomatoes outdoors."

574
01:04:03.340 --> 01:04:05.840
It's a miss this year.

575
01:04:13.670 --> 01:04:15.250
Are there snails around you?

576
01:04:15.920 --> 01:04:17.380
I don't see any here.

577
01:04:17.710 --> 01:04:19.710
Hae-won! How much did you catch?

578
01:04:20.150 --> 01:04:22.400
You wanna see?

579
01:04:25.190 --> 01:04:27.270
Ow! My eyes!

580
01:04:28.980 --> 01:04:30.560
There's a lot here!

581
01:04:31.480 --> 01:04:33.020
There's a lot here too!

582
01:04:46.850 --> 01:04:48.440
Did that to your boyfriend too?

583
01:04:49.520 --> 01:04:50.520
What?

584
01:04:51.270 --> 01:04:53.270
Stare at him when he's eating?

585
01:04:57.770 --> 01:04:59.150
Why do you ask?

586
01:05:00.400 --> 01:05:01.650
Just because.

587
01:05:02.480 --> 01:05:03.850
Is it uncomfortable?

588
01:05:04.810 --> 01:05:06.810
Sometimes it's uncomfortable.

589
01:05:07.060 --> 01:05:08.890
You retard!

590
01:05:08.900 --> 01:05:13.350
"What girl makes lunch
for her boyfriend these days?"

591
01:05:13.690 --> 01:05:16.650
"That's only on TV, pal.
No one does that."

592
01:05:16.950 --> 01:05:19.080
I wish she'd study instead.

593
01:05:19.080 --> 01:05:20.950
Don't complain, pal.

594
01:05:21.410 --> 01:05:23.250
I stopped after that.

595
01:05:24.160 --> 01:05:26.330
He was probably bragging.

596
01:05:27.200 --> 01:05:29.700
But I felt horrible.

597
01:05:31.830 --> 01:05:33.200
That's why you broke up?

598
01:05:34.660 --> 01:05:35.660
What?

599
01:05:38.620 --> 01:05:39.950
We didn't break up.

600
01:05:45.040 --> 01:05:46.450
Why'd you break up?

601
01:05:46.450 --> 01:05:47.660
Who says I did?

602
01:05:48.700 --> 01:05:49.740
Eun-sook.

603
01:05:49.750 --> 01:05:51.040
Why would she..!

604
01:05:54.700 --> 01:05:55.700
You know,

605
01:05:57.580 --> 01:06:00.700
I came back here and she's there.

606
01:06:01.660 --> 01:06:03.450
You're so cool about it.

607
01:06:03.660 --> 01:06:04.950
No. I cried a lot.

608
01:06:07.410 --> 01:06:08.410
Really?

609
01:06:08.620 --> 01:06:10.120
I balled when we broke up.

610
01:06:13.410 --> 01:06:18.500
"Leaving Seoul wasn't hard,
but leaving her was painful."

611
01:06:20.370 --> 01:06:22.000
I really liked her a lot.

612
01:06:24.330 --> 01:06:26.000
"What did you say
when you broke up?"

613
01:06:29.200 --> 01:06:31.790
"That I didn't want
to take orders from others."

614
01:06:36.700 --> 01:06:38.700
Were you drunk?

615
01:06:40.750 --> 01:06:42.410
Working for a company,

616
01:06:45.620 --> 01:06:48.410
"there was nothing
I could decide on my own."

617
01:06:52.700 --> 01:06:56.700
"I had no time to think
or live a life."

618
01:06:57.120 --> 01:06:59.790
"Just waiting for payday
to come around..."

619
01:07:01.620 --> 01:07:03.120
Suddenly, it hit me.

620
01:07:03.950 --> 01:07:09.200
"Seeing myself live like that,
I felt like I'd go crazy."

621
01:07:12.580 --> 01:07:14.040
So, what did she say?

622
01:07:14.580 --> 01:07:15.580
What?

623
01:07:17.910 --> 01:07:23.160
"She didn't believe me.
She said good luck with the bitch."

624
01:07:24.000 --> 01:07:27.250
I'm here!

625
01:07:28.450 --> 01:07:30.080
What did she bring?

626
01:07:30.660 --> 01:07:32.750
"What are you doing?
Having fun?"

627
01:07:33.240 --> 01:07:35.240
Don't have fun without me!

628
01:07:36.320 --> 01:07:37.610
It's slippery here!

629
01:07:38.360 --> 01:07:40.360
"- What's that?
- So heavy!"

630
01:07:41.450 --> 01:07:44.530
"I stole it while my dad
went into town!"

631
01:07:45.820 --> 01:07:47.610
If you get caught, you're dead!

632
01:07:47.610 --> 01:07:51.650
"I'll just fill it up with water.
There's lots here!"

633
01:07:52.070 --> 01:07:54.820
"Why'd you bring that?
To drink it all?"

634
01:07:55.490 --> 01:07:58.450
Yes! Let's drink till we drop!

635
01:07:58.570 --> 01:07:59.570
Why?

636
01:07:59.570 --> 01:08:03.240
"My damn manager isn't moving
to another branch now!"

637
01:08:03.780 --> 01:08:06.990
"I put up with him because
I thought he'd be gone soon."

638
01:08:07.320 --> 01:08:10.070
"I'm so mad!
I don't know what to do!"

639
01:08:10.280 --> 01:08:11.450
Give me a cup.

640
01:08:13.610 --> 01:08:15.740
"No one leaves
until we finish this!"

641
01:08:18.490 --> 01:08:19.280
Hey.

642
01:08:19.280 --> 01:08:21.450
It's not balloon flower root.

643
01:08:22.990 --> 01:08:28.530
Dad used to farm bodark trees.

644
01:08:29.070 --> 01:08:30.900
Gross!

645
01:08:30.900 --> 01:08:32.900
"- Bodark?
- Come on."

646
01:08:33.280 --> 01:08:35.280
"- Bodark bark!
- Stop it!"

647
01:08:37.070 --> 01:08:39.610
Bodark bark! Woof!

648
01:08:41.820 --> 01:08:46.280
Don't spit on me! Gross!

649
01:09:06.400 --> 01:09:07.400
Hoon?

650
01:09:07.860 --> 01:09:09.610
I was going to call you.

651
01:09:09.610 --> 01:09:10.950
It's been a while.

652
01:09:12.280 --> 01:09:13.280
I know.

653
01:09:15.740 --> 01:09:18.990
I've been meaning to say this.

654
01:09:19.860 --> 01:09:22.450
To break up?

655
01:09:23.450 --> 01:09:24.780
That too.

656
01:09:29.200 --> 01:09:31.070
I know it's really late,

657
01:09:33.530 --> 01:09:38.820
"but congratulations
on your exam."

658
01:09:39.360 --> 01:09:40.530
Thanks.

659
01:09:41.650 --> 01:09:45.490
"I don't remember
what I said after that."

660
01:09:46.530 --> 01:09:48.400
But I remember one thing.

661
01:09:49.070 --> 01:09:53.070
"I said I didn't leave for here,
but that I came back."

662
01:10:18.160 --> 01:10:19.960
Yes! I won!

663
01:10:27.110 --> 01:10:33.400
AUTUMN

664
01:10:41.740 --> 01:10:43.490
"- Hey!
- Hi."

665
01:10:43.490 --> 01:10:45.490
"- Withdrew money?
- Yup."

666
01:10:45.900 --> 01:10:47.560
Anything left in your balance?

667
01:10:47.690 --> 01:10:50.060
My balance is a lot! Not.

668
01:10:52.730 --> 01:10:56.150
"Don't go to loan sharks
if you're empty."

669
01:10:56.310 --> 01:10:58.310
"- Come to me, okay?
- Sure."

670
01:10:58.480 --> 01:11:00.560
"- They're scary!
- I know."

671
01:11:00.810 --> 01:11:06.980
"Should we call Jae-ha
and eat out in town?"

672
01:11:10.020 --> 01:11:12.100
He's working. Why call him?

673
01:11:13.150 --> 01:11:15.980
"Did you tell Jae-ha
that you like him yet?"

674
01:11:18.310 --> 01:11:21.560
"After everything I did,
he should know."

675
01:11:23.560 --> 01:11:26.100
"If you don't say anything,
how would he know?"

676
01:11:26.480 --> 01:11:28.560
Don't start preaching again.

677
01:11:28.810 --> 01:11:29.900
Got that?

678
01:11:33.560 --> 01:11:37.060
"They don't know
if you just keep quiet and patient."

679
01:11:37.810 --> 01:11:40.900
"You have to spit it out
or it'll rot inside you."

680
01:11:41.810 --> 01:11:43.350
"- See ya.
- Bye!"

681
01:11:43.350 --> 01:11:48.230
"That's what I told her,
but I couldn't do it either."

682
01:11:49.060 --> 01:11:53.900
"This card was denied, sir.
Do you have cash or another card?"

683
01:11:53.940 --> 01:11:57.270
"Who carries cash around
these days?"

684
01:11:57.270 --> 01:11:59.440
I just used it at another store!

685
01:11:59.440 --> 01:12:03.190
"Swipe it again!
Call the manager out!"

686
01:12:03.190 --> 01:12:06.770
I just took it in.

687
01:12:07.270 --> 01:12:09.600
You good for nothing twerp!

688
01:12:10.350 --> 01:12:14.480
"Stop wasting company money
and work for your pay!"

689
01:12:15.810 --> 01:12:18.480
"What kind of irresponsible dork
are you!"

690
01:12:20.980 --> 01:12:21.980
What?

691
01:12:22.440 --> 01:12:24.810
What are you doing?

692
01:12:26.480 --> 01:12:28.480
I didn't reject it like Jae-ha.

693
01:12:28.730 --> 01:12:35.270
You are my special love.

694
01:12:37.270 --> 01:12:43.100
"I'd cross the Pacific
and Atlantic oceans for you."

695
01:12:44.100 --> 01:12:47.520
If you call me, I'll run to you.

696
01:12:47.560 --> 01:12:50.150
"Eun-sook's not one
to keep things bottled up."

697
01:12:51.020 --> 01:12:55.060
"She hit her manager's head
with a tambourine before payday."

698
01:12:55.650 --> 01:13:01.020
"Luckily, she got her pay and
the manager went to another branch."

699
01:13:01.910 --> 01:13:05.580
"Now, I'm the only one
Eun-sook needs out of the way."

700
01:13:05.700 --> 01:13:06.700
What?

701
01:13:10.500 --> 01:13:13.370
"If you don't leave here,
I won't either."

702
01:13:14.580 --> 01:13:15.580
What?

703
01:13:16.750 --> 01:13:19.290
"Let's fight fair and square
over Jae-ha."

704
01:13:21.040 --> 01:13:22.450
What do you mean?

705
01:13:22.620 --> 01:13:23.910
Think you'll lose?

706
01:13:26.250 --> 01:13:27.250
What?

707
01:13:27.370 --> 01:13:28.700
Okay...

708
01:13:31.000 --> 01:13:32.370
"- Holy!
- Deal."

709
01:13:38.450 --> 01:13:39.790
I don't believe this!

710
01:13:45.410 --> 01:13:48.250
She was Jae-ha's ex-girlfriend.

711
01:13:57.890 --> 01:14:00.800
I was barking up the wrong tree.

712
01:14:05.470 --> 01:14:07.470
Our ancestors were amazing.

713
01:14:08.470 --> 01:14:12.220
"They made that idiom
to explain my situation now."

714
01:14:14.010 --> 01:14:15.220
Will you give up?

715
01:14:21.640 --> 01:14:23.300
Her skin is too white.

716
01:14:25.220 --> 01:14:26.850
I don't stand a chance.

717
01:14:29.510 --> 01:14:33.100
It could be the right tree.

718
01:14:34.010 --> 01:14:37.350
"Don't give up barking.
Once the prey comes down, catch it."

719
01:14:38.510 --> 01:14:40.140
I'm so stressed!

720
01:14:41.680 --> 01:14:42.970
Got anything to eat?

721
01:14:43.470 --> 01:14:48.680
"You said if I hit the manager,
you'd give me the best food."

722
01:14:50.720 --> 01:14:51.720
I did?

723
01:14:54.430 --> 01:14:58.180
"The best food is making it
yourself."

724
01:15:05.680 --> 01:15:08.180
Not the cabbage, but peppers.

725
01:15:10.430 --> 01:15:11.600
Peppers.

726
01:15:12.350 --> 01:15:15.180
"That's too much!
It'll rip up our stomach!"

727
01:15:16.140 --> 01:15:18.220
I'll eat spicy food and die!

728
01:15:47.600 --> 01:15:48.720
Is it good?

729
01:15:49.050 --> 01:15:50.050
Totally!

730
01:15:56.010 --> 01:15:57.430
Did you two fight?

731
01:16:03.220 --> 01:16:04.350
It's spicy.

732
01:16:06.510 --> 01:16:08.220
"I'm crying more than
when I got dumped."

733
01:16:10.600 --> 01:16:12.600
Get your own fork!

734
01:16:17.050 --> 01:16:19.350
"- Where's the girl?
- She left."

735
01:16:20.720 --> 01:16:22.390
Already? Did you fight?

736
01:16:23.930 --> 01:16:25.680
She was just dropping by.

737
01:16:26.220 --> 01:16:30.890
"Why would she drop by
a rural place like this?"

738
01:16:32.180 --> 01:16:35.600
"Why'd she have to come now
when I'm over her?"

739
01:16:40.390 --> 01:16:42.050
Are you crying?

740
01:16:44.930 --> 01:16:46.350
It's because it's spicy.

741
01:16:48.430 --> 01:16:53.300
"I heard later Jae-ha's ex-girlfriend
was not over him."

742
01:16:55.100 --> 01:16:57.100
But Jae-ha said to her...

743
01:17:01.010 --> 01:17:03.010
I like someone else now.

744
01:17:34.100 --> 01:17:37.390
"As a child,
I heard bears came out in the fall."

745
01:17:39.260 --> 01:17:43.220
"Though it can't be true,
memories have lasting impacts."

746
01:18:01.630 --> 01:18:02.880
See you tomorrow.

747
01:19:13.070 --> 01:19:15.900
"I make sweet chestnuts
even sweeter to store them,"

748
01:19:16.950 --> 01:19:21.200
"so that I won't eat them
all at once."

749
01:19:47.950 --> 01:19:52.650
"Glazed chestnuts tasting this good
means it is deep into autumn."

750
01:20:06.490 --> 01:20:09.200
"My friend Jae-ha
the soon-to-be millionaire!"

751
01:20:10.490 --> 01:20:12.780
Your paddy is filled with rice.

752
01:20:13.110 --> 01:20:16.780
"Your orchard
is covered with apples."

753
01:20:17.450 --> 01:20:19.900
The rice paddy is my dad's.

754
01:20:20.740 --> 01:20:21.740
Still...

755
01:20:22.460 --> 01:20:25.170
"I'll give you a sack of rice
at harvest, if..."

756
01:20:25.590 --> 01:20:26.420
If what?

757
01:20:26.420 --> 01:20:29.000
"Help pick the apples.
Stop loafing around."

758
01:20:29.090 --> 01:20:31.880
What? I keep busy!

759
01:20:32.340 --> 01:20:35.960
"I have to help my aunt
pick peppers and sesame."

760
01:20:36.210 --> 01:20:39.130
"I have to find chestnuts
and dry persimmons too."

761
01:20:39.130 --> 01:20:40.960
I have lots to do.

762
01:20:41.920 --> 01:20:47.170
"You say you'll go to Seoul,
but you're busy storing fall's goods?"

763
01:20:49.000 --> 01:20:51.380
"Keeping busy like that
won't solve your problems."

764
01:21:03.380 --> 01:21:04.380
Right.

765
01:21:05.380 --> 01:21:09.000
"I should go back soon
and figure out my life, right?"

766
01:21:11.630 --> 01:21:12.630
See ya!

767
01:21:29.340 --> 01:21:30.340
Damn it!

768
01:22:01.800 --> 01:22:03.880
Why are you out in the rain?

769
01:22:07.380 --> 01:22:08.630
Were you scared?

770
01:22:11.090 --> 01:22:12.340
It's okay. I'm here.

771
01:22:44.550 --> 01:22:47.800
"I called in a tractor
to harvest next week."

772
01:22:50.130 --> 01:22:52.000
Heaven can be cruel.

773
01:22:54.370 --> 01:22:56.830
"You worked so hard
in the scorching heat..."

774
01:22:58.450 --> 01:22:59.910
It's not fair.

775
01:23:00.620 --> 01:23:05.950
"What can we do against
heaven's will?"

776
01:23:12.160 --> 01:23:13.870
Don't work too hard.

777
01:23:35.120 --> 01:23:38.330
I should've gone back yesterday.

778
01:23:40.910 --> 01:23:43.750
We'll never get this done!

779
01:23:46.080 --> 01:23:52.290
"Stop yapping and work!
We'll be done soon."

780
01:23:52.660 --> 01:23:54.080
It's endless!

781
01:23:54.370 --> 01:23:56.370
Ow! My back!

782
01:24:28.370 --> 01:24:30.000
The storm hit here too?

783
01:24:30.540 --> 01:24:32.160
"- Hi.
- Too bad."

784
01:24:33.950 --> 01:24:37.500
"Lesson learned
for a newbie farmer."

785
01:24:39.450 --> 01:24:44.000
"You enjoy living like this
when farming is this hard?"

786
01:24:47.290 --> 01:24:52.290
"Getting hit hard like this
is upsetting,"

787
01:24:53.450 --> 01:24:55.290
but farming suits me.

788
01:24:56.790 --> 01:25:00.290
"At least there's no scamming
or cheating in farming."

789
01:25:02.750 --> 01:25:04.830
"My body may hurt,
but I'm not stressed."

790
01:25:12.040 --> 01:25:13.040
What's wrong?

791
01:25:14.610 --> 01:25:17.780
I put up rice stalks yesterday.

792
01:25:19.360 --> 01:25:21.360
You're in pain just from that?

793
01:25:22.150 --> 01:25:25.780
What? I almost died!

794
01:25:26.650 --> 01:25:30.990
"Wish I can show you my back
covered with pain relief patches."

795
01:25:31.490 --> 01:25:33.150
Ow! My back!

796
01:25:33.320 --> 01:25:35.070
Just go home.

797
01:25:36.360 --> 01:25:38.820
Take some fallen apples with you.

798
01:25:38.900 --> 01:25:40.900
Make apple jam with them.

799
01:25:41.280 --> 01:25:42.610
Can I really go?

800
01:25:43.150 --> 01:25:44.450
Yes!

801
01:25:45.900 --> 01:25:47.700
It's better if you go.

802
01:25:57.990 --> 01:25:58.990
Wait!

803
01:26:00.320 --> 01:26:01.320
Take this.

804
01:26:03.860 --> 01:26:05.360
This apple is fine.

805
01:26:05.990 --> 01:26:08.320
"I wanted to give you that
before this."

806
01:26:09.070 --> 01:26:11.400
"It held out through
the typhoon."

807
01:26:11.400 --> 01:26:12.490
Unlike you.

808
01:26:53.740 --> 01:26:55.150
Jae-ha was right.

809
01:26:56.030 --> 01:26:57.900
I ignore what's important

810
01:26:57.900 --> 01:27:02.030
"and evade the problem
by pretending to work hard."

811
01:27:07.400 --> 01:27:10.820
You chose this life not me.

812
01:27:11.240 --> 01:27:12.950
What will you do in the city?

813
01:27:13.490 --> 01:27:16.700
"What's to do here?
Cooking and plucking weed?"

814
01:27:17.280 --> 01:27:20.320
"You may want to live here forever,
but not me!"

815
01:27:22.030 --> 01:27:27.900
"If you massage it, it'll become
a soft dried persimmon in winter."

816
01:27:30.150 --> 01:27:35.950
"Winter has to come
to eat good dried persimmon."

817
01:27:37.560 --> 01:27:38.690
What in the world!

818
01:27:46.770 --> 01:27:48.190
I'm going to school.

819
01:27:48.520 --> 01:27:49.650
Eat before you go.

820
01:27:49.900 --> 01:27:51.560
Mom, I'm late!

821
01:27:52.060 --> 01:27:55.650
"I'm going to live right next to
a bus stop in Seoul."

822
01:27:57.230 --> 01:27:59.850
"And it's less cold in Seoul.
Bye!"

823
01:28:30.400 --> 01:28:34.400
"Hae-won, you'll leave here
for college soon."

824
01:28:35.650 --> 01:28:42.520
"I want to go and try things that
I had given up to get married early."

825
01:28:44.020 --> 01:28:48.900
"I may fail, and I'm worried
that it may be too late,"

826
01:28:49.810 --> 01:28:54.980
"but I'll walk out our front gate
and make my own time."

827
01:28:56.400 --> 01:28:59.690
"I always said everything
is about timing."

828
01:29:00.440 --> 01:29:02.940
I think the time has come now.

829
01:29:04.520 --> 01:29:09.190
"I didn't go back to Seoul
after your dad passed away"

830
01:29:10.230 --> 01:29:14.600
"because I wanted to plant
and have you set root here."

831
01:29:16.190 --> 01:29:18.190
When things are hard,

832
01:29:18.560 --> 01:29:23.270
"remember the scent of the land,
the wind and sun here."

833
01:29:24.480 --> 01:29:29.480
"Then I know you can dust yourself off
and get up again."

834
01:29:31.770 --> 01:29:40.100
"Let's think of it as the start
of a long trip to return home well."

835
01:29:45.480 --> 01:29:49.850
"I love you always, Hae-won.
From Mom."

836
01:29:55.770 --> 01:29:59.560
Finally, I understand Mom's letter.

837
01:30:10.020 --> 01:30:11.020
Mom?

838
01:30:12.810 --> 01:30:13.810
Mom?

839
01:30:15.560 --> 01:30:17.350
Where are you?

840
01:30:18.600 --> 01:30:19.850
Mom?

841
01:30:29.400 --> 01:30:30.900
For Mom,

842
01:30:31.310 --> 01:30:34.560
"the nature, cooking,
and her love for me"

843
01:30:35.230 --> 01:30:37.230
have been her little forest.

844
01:30:39.940 --> 01:30:44.480
"I should find
my own little forest too."

845
01:30:52.020 --> 01:30:54.400
I wrote back to Mom that night.

846
01:31:52.560 --> 01:31:54.560
Dear Mom,

847
01:32:50.900 --> 01:32:53.230
"If dried persimmons
taste this good,"

848
01:32:54.940 --> 01:32:57.230
it means it is deep into winter.

849
01:33:27.310 --> 01:33:30.400
"Whoever sees this first
takes care of Fivo and the hen."

850
01:33:39.440 --> 01:33:42.900
"She makes me so mad.
How can she not call once?"

851
01:33:45.470 --> 01:33:48.220
"She's like a salary
passing through a bankbook."

852
01:33:49.390 --> 01:33:53.600
"You think she'd stay,
but vanishes in a flash."

853
01:33:55.680 --> 01:33:57.350
I don't think she ran away.

854
01:33:57.600 --> 01:33:58.600
What?

855
01:33:59.010 --> 01:34:01.430
Are you two keeping in touch?

856
01:34:02.300 --> 01:34:06.390
"I just have a feeling
Hae-won will be back soon."

857
01:34:06.970 --> 01:34:08.390
Really? Why?

858
01:34:09.720 --> 01:34:10.930
Permanent planting.

859
01:34:12.300 --> 01:34:15.970
"Maybe Hae-won is preparing for
permanent planting."

860
01:34:32.260 --> 01:34:34.930
Onions start out as seeds.

861
01:34:36.850 --> 01:34:39.850
Plant the seeds in the fall.

862
01:34:40.180 --> 01:34:44.890
"Cover it for a week with a straw mat
until the sprouts grow."

863
01:34:50.470 --> 01:34:55.390
"Then you move and plant them
in a good, fertilized field."

864
01:34:56.550 --> 01:34:58.710
That's permanent planting.

865
01:34:59.710 --> 01:35:03.380
"It means no transplanting,
but planting for good."

866
01:35:08.460 --> 01:35:12.050
"If you protect them
until they set root,"

867
01:35:12.590 --> 01:35:16.250
"they won't die and wither
in the frost."

868
01:35:16.630 --> 01:35:22.050
"Onions that endured winter
are sweeter than spring onions."

869
01:35:26.300 --> 01:35:31.090
"Hope she knows we did this
for her in the cold!"

870
01:35:32.380 --> 01:35:33.840
It's freezing!

871
01:35:45.960 --> 01:35:48.590
"Here's your order of
salad rice bowl."

872
01:35:48.880 --> 01:35:50.840
"Let me know if you need
anything else."

873
01:35:50.840 --> 01:35:51.840
Thank you.

874
01:35:53.050 --> 01:35:54.750
"- Water, please.
- Yes."

875
01:36:20.800 --> 01:36:22.000
It's spring!

876
01:37:53.420 --> 01:37:54.420
Fivo!

877
01:37:56.750 --> 01:37:58.750
Fivo! I missed you!

878
01:37:59.340 --> 01:38:01.710
How'd you come here?

879
01:38:12.340 --> 01:38:13.340
Fivo!

880
01:39:30.640 --> 01:39:32.020
Hello!
